  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nuevas narrativas locales para combatir la desinformaci&#xbf;n y la estigmatizaci&#xbf;n sobre la acci&#xbf;n de defensa de los derechos humanos y el periodismo comunitario en Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;Even though Colombia is among the longest-standing democracies in Latin America, it still presents a complex human rights and freedom of expression context as well as a history of violence and human rights abuses. The use of populist disinformation campaigns and strategies that present some people and groups as `enemies&#xbf; contributes to the creation of a dangerous environment for the exercise of political activities and other activities related to the political life of the country, such as journalism and the defense of human rights. In the context of the peace agreements and the upcoming elections, polarization has been on the rise. Within this setting, an increasing number of media outlets, journalists and civil society organizations are now vigilant about these phenomena and provide prompt verification, including fact-checking. There exist identified CSOs active and capable of managing&amp;nbsp;EU support to pursue their efforts in the two sub-themes proposed below.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Actions aimed at strengthening democracy and stabilization are already underway with support from the EU Delegation and EU Member States. At present there are however no specific actions on the issue of Media and Conflict, which is politically highly relevant to justify FPI support.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
